{
  /* The service worker runs in a WebWorker scope: `self` is a
     `ServiceWorkerGlobalScope`, there is no `window`, and the DOM lib's own
     `self` would shadow it. Its own project, so the app keeps DOM types and the
     worker keeps worker types. */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.worker.tsbuildinfo",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "WebWorker"],
    "types": ["vite/client"]
  },
  /* **Overridden, not inherited**, for the reason `tsconfig.test.json` says at
     more length: `extends` merges `exclude`, and the app's names `src/sw.ts` —
     the very file this project exists for. Without this the worker resolves to
     everything *except* the worker, so the one file already outside the coverage
     profile (jsdom cannot enter a WebWorker scope) had no typechecker either.
     Empty for the reason `tsconfig.test.json` gives: the defaults this also
     discards cannot match an `src/`-rooted include. */
  "exclude": [],
  "include": ["src/sw.ts", "src/lib/pushMessage.ts", "src/lib/pushOpen.ts"]
}
